  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Amylopectin is insoluble in water and constitutes about 80-85% starch.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0145_f1adfa04662b.png\" /></p><p>Amylopectin is a water-soluble polysaccharide and highly branched polymer of a-glucose units found in plants. It is one of the two components of starch, the other being amylose. Amylopectin bears a straight/linear chain along with a number of side chains which may be branched further.</p>"
